A('1965-0207-donghoi', '1965-02-07', VH, 'Quảng Bình. Feb. 7 the Air Defense–Air Force command, on the Politburo\'s and the Central Military Party Committee\'s alert, puts units on alert from early morning. At 1:53 p.m. the radar of Company 2, Radar Regiment 290 (Lương Hữu Sắt, Nguyễn Đặng Tuất), picks up the first flight, from the Phú Hội dunes, bombing Đồng Hới town. The antiaircraft guns of the 325th and 341st Infantry Divisions, two navy patrol boats at Nhật Lệ and the militia shoot down three American aircraft, by the history\'s count.', 'III, 404–05', time='13:53', tz='Asia/Bangkok', place='dong-hoi', names=['Lương Hữu Sắt', 'Nguyễn Đặng Tuất'], also=AW, check='the clock; the American record not read ([[cal.1965-02-07.vietnam]] has the day\'s strikes).')
A('1965-0208-hoxa', '1965-02-08', VH, 'Quảng Bình. Feb. 8 American aircraft with the South Vietnamese air force under Nguyễn Cao Kỳ strike Hồ Xá, Vĩnh Linh, and Đồng Hới town. The air defense of the two areas, warned in time, shoots down three over Vĩnh Linh and two over Đồng Hới: eight in the two days, by the history\'s count. The 37-mm battalion of Lại Đạt and Nguyễn Nghị goes from Vinh to Đồng Hới; Regiment 234\'s 14.5-mm machine guns and two battalions of the artillery officers\' school go to Vĩnh Linh and Quảng Bình.', 'III, 405–06', place='ho-xa', names=['Nguyễn Cao Kỳ'], also=AW, check='the American record not read; the place field takes the first target.')
A('1965-0211-hoxa', '1965-02-11', VH, 'Quảng Bình. Feb. 11 American aircraft hit Hồ Xá, the Vĩnh Linh area, Cồn Cỏ island, Đồng Hới and near places. The air defense shoots down an F8U and takes the pilot, Maj. Robert Shumaker, on Lý Ninh hill; at the Gianh port Company 54 and the machine-gun units, the river fishermen\'s self-defense and the militia down two. Quảng Bình\'s total for the day: six aircraft, by the history\'s count.', 'III, 406', place='ho-xa', also=AW, check='the pilot\'s name is printed in the history in Vietnamese transcription ("Rôbơt Sumếchcơ"); the American record not read.')
A('1965-0403-hamrong', '1965-04-03', VH, 'Thanh Hóa. Apr. 3, the Air Defense–Air Force command having decided the night before to use fighters at the Hàm Rồng bridge, American aircraft bomb the Đò Lèn bridge in the morning; the antiaircraft of Regiment 234 and the local forces shoot down an F4 in the first minute. At 10 a.m. they bomb the Hàm Rồng bridge area, and two flights of MiG-17s of the 921st Fighter Regiment, under Phạm Ngọc Lan and Trần Hanh, go up with the ground defense: after a flight of 20 minutes they have shot down two F8s and return safe. At 12:50 p.m. a second raid on the bridge; the antiaircraft fights nearly two hours, a militia machine-gun crew under Phạm Gia Huấn downs a plane. Eight American aircraft down in the day, by the history\'s count. Apr. 3 becomes the day of the Vietnamese People\'s Air Force.', 'III, 410', time='10:00', tz='Asia/Bangkok', place='ham-rong', names=['Phạm Ngọc Lan', 'Trần Hanh', 'Phạm Gia Huấn'], also=AW, check='the American record ([[cal.1965-04-03.vietnam]]) has the two F-105s lost to MiGs on Apr. 4, not F-8s on Apr. 3; the clock times are Hanoi\'s.')
A('1965-0404-phaghep', '1965-04-04', VH, 'Thanh Hóa. Apr. 4, at 8:20 a.m., American aircraft bomb the Ghép ferry on the Yên River, as three antiaircraft companies of Regiment 234 from Nghệ An, sent overnight to the Hàm Rồng, are crossing: the guns are fired from their tow vehicles. Thirty minutes: three aircraft shot down, a pilot taken. At 9:30 a.m. a second raid: Companies 2 and 5 of the regiment and a machine-gun crew, with the militia of both banks, set seven aircraft afire, by the history\'s count.', 'III, 411', time='08:20', tz='Asia/Bangkok', place='pha-ghep', also=AW, check='the clock; the history gives Hanoi\'s hours; the American record not read.')
A('1965-0404-hamrong', '1965-04-04', VH, 'Thanh Hóa. Apr. 4 American aircraft raid the Hàm Rồng bridge in waves: at 8:30 a.m. an F-105 is shot down at once; at 9:30 a second raid; at 10:05 a third, driven off by the fire of patrol boats 120 and 186 and the batteries of Regiments 228, 280 and 234 and the militia, the bombs falling at random on the villages. A flight under Trần Hanh attacks the rear of the F-105s and in four minutes of air fighting shoots down two. The bridge stands.', 'III, 411–12', time='08:30', tz='Asia/Bangkok', place='ham-rong', names=['Trần Hanh'], also=AW, check='the clock; the American record has two F-105s lost to MiGs, Apr. 4 ([[cal.1965-04-03.vietnam]], [[cal.1965-04-04.vietnam-air-war]]).')
A('1965-0221-sau', '1965-02-21', 'vietnam-saigon', 'Saigon. Phan Khắc Sửu, chief of state, signs a decree naming Trần Văn Minh acting commander in chief in Nguyễn Khánh\'s place, Feb. 21, under pressure of the young generals who overthrew Khánh the day before. Khánh is out after 13 months.', 'III, 395', place='saigon', names=['Phan Khắc Sửu', 'Trần Văn Minh', 'Nguyễn Khánh'], also=['vietnam'], tags=['polity:rvn'], check='the American record not read; compare [[cal.1965-02-20.vietnam-saigon]].')
